+# DSH Testkit Release Report
+
+Version: v0.1
+Status: Ready_For_User_Review
+Last updated: 2026-08-15
+
+## Release Scope
+
+The `lifecycle-runner` MVP is complete in the local repository. It delivers the `dsh-test` CLI, Docker-default and explicit unsafe-local runners, the exact DSH npm adapter, runtime probe, lifecycle fixtures, canonical reports, published JSON schemas, a composite GitHub Action and contributor documentation. No repository, npm package, image or release tag has been published.
+
+## Verification
+
+| Gate | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `pnpm validate` | Passed: typecheck, build, 9 test files and 41 tests |
+| Real DSH E2E | Passed: 5 fixtures against `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.0-rc.6` in 227.35 s |
+| Default Docker path | Passed on Linux arm64, Node v22.23.2, pnpm 11.1.3 |
+| Packed consumer | Passed, including a Docker image build from the installed tarball |
+| Production dependency audit | No known vulnerabilities from the public npm registry |
+| Delivery artifact validator | Passed with all three governed tasks and evidence bundles present |
+
+The final Docker proof is `/tmp/dsh-testkit-docker-release-final-20260815/report.json`. It binds the scenario snapshot, plugin tarball, DSH package tree and runner image by SHA-256, confirms no process or listener beyond the container baseline, removes the owned run root and leaves no active Testkit container.
+
+## Review
+
+- Spec compliance: Pass for the locally deliverable MVP requirements and acceptance fixtures.
+- Engineering quality: Pass. The controller does not load plugin code; output paths, artifacts, logs, timeouts, process groups and container resources are bounded and checked.
+- QA acceptance: Pass for repository-owned validation, real-host fixtures, Docker execution and packed consumption.
+- User acceptance: Pending. Governed tasks remain `Needs_Review`.
+
+## Field Success Criteria
+
+- Verified locally: SC-005, SC-006, SC-007, SC-008 and the repository-native design required by SC-010.
+- Requires public field work: SC-001 ten community plugins, SC-002 three upstream lifecycle findings, SC-003 external CI adoption, SC-004 five-run consistency measurement and SC-009 a private enterprise repository proof.
+- The `flaky` verdict and exit code are stable contracts; multi-run aggregation is not a v0.1 CLI workflow.
+- Network tracing is unavailable in v0.1. A scenario that requires it returns `unsupported`.
+
+## Publication Gate
+
+Publishing to GitHub, npm or a container registry requires explicit user approval after this review. The npm name `dsh-testkit` returned `404 Not Found` from the public registry on 2026-08-15, but availability is not reserved until publication.
